{"name":"Tree House","hex":"#3b2820","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tree house","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of treehouse."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tree_house"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tree House, Crawley","blocks":[{"text":"Tree House, also known as The Tree, is a medieval timber-framed house on the High Street in Crawley, a town and borough in West Sussex, England. It is the original manor house of Crawley, and was built in the early 15th century and rebuilt in the mid-16th century. It now has a modern exterior, but the old structure is still in place inside. Situated in a prominent position facing both the High Street and The Boulevard, two of Crawley town centre's main roads, its name commemorates an ancient elm tree which stood outside for hundreds of years and was one of Crawley's landmarks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Tree_House%2C_103_High_Street%2C_Crawley.JPG/330px-Tree_House%2C_103_High_Street%2C_Crawley.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree_House%2C_Crawley"},{"title":"Tree house","blocks":[{"text":"A tree house, tree fort or tree shed, is a platform or building constructed around, next to or among the trunk or branches of one or more mature trees while above ground level. Tree houses can be used for recreation, work space, habitation, a hangout space and observation. People occasionally connect ladders or staircases to get up to the platforms."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Arba_domo_en_la_parko_de_la_Ch%C3%A2teau_de_Langeais_02.jpg/330px-Arba_domo_en_la_parko_de_la_Ch%C3%A2teau_de_Langeais_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree_house"},{"title":"Tree House (Le1f mixtape)","blocks":[{"text":"Tree House is the third mixtape by American rapper and producer Le1f. It was released on Camp & Street on September 18, 2013."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b9/Tree_House_%28Le1f_mixtape%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree_House_(Le1f_mixtape)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Tree_House%2C_103_High_Street%2C_Crawley.JPG/500px-Tree_House%2C_103_High_Street%2C_Crawley.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Tree_House%2C_103_High_Street%2C_Crawley.JPG/1280px-Tree_House%2C_103_High_Street%2C_Crawley.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Tree_House%2C_103_High_Street%2C_Crawley.JPG/500px-Tree_House%2C_103_High_Street%2C_Crawley.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATree_House%2C_103_High_Street%2C_Crawley.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/John_Leech_Plaque_at_Tree_House%2C_Crawley.jpg/330px-John_Leech_Plaque_at_Tree_House%2C_Crawley.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/John_Leech_Plaque_at_Tree_House%2C_Crawley.jpg/330px-John_Leech_Plaque_at_Tree_House%2C_Crawley.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Commemorative plaque recording John Leech's residence","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJohn_Leech_Plaque_at_Tree_House%2C_Crawley.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Tree_House%2C_103_High_Street%2C_Crawley_%28South_Face%29_%28IoE_Code_363351%29.JPG/500px-Tree_House%2C_103_High_Street%2C_Crawley_%28South_Face%29_%28IoE_Code_363351%29.JPG?utm_